# rz2 -> rzir front-end resolver, N LETS, multi-char names, authored in M0.
# Loops over N const-lets emitting `  vK: i32 = const VAL` per let (K = a digit),
# then the return op line, resolving each operand to its vN by re-scanning the
# lets for the matching name (streq). Handles 2 or 3+ lets; the result/ret var is
# vN where N = number of lets. Contingent: single-digit vN (<10 lets). Builds
# output in OUT, one final write. Chain: hex2 -> M0 -> this. No cc.
#
# bss: INBUF 0x440000, OUT 0x450000; NCOUNT 0x460000, A_S 0x460008, A_L 0x460010,
#      B_S 0x460018, B_L 0x460020.

# === instruction-encoding library ===
